Available tool reference:
{
  "add_generative_widget": {
    "args": {
      "chart_params": "object with chartType, xKey, yKey for chart",
      "dashboard_id": "string UUID from tool result only, optional; omit for active dashboard",
      "data": "string for note/html; array for table/chart",
      "description": "string, optional",
      "inner_tab": "string tab id, optional",
      "name": "string, optional",
      "widget_type": "note|table|chart|html"
    },
    "description": "Add generated note, table, chart, or HTML widget."
  },
  "get_workspace_snapshot": {
    "args": {},
    "description": "Inspect current dashboard, tabs, widgets, layouts, and backends."
  },
  "manage_apps": {
    "args": {
      "activate": "boolean, optional",
      "app_name": "string, optional",
      "backend_id": "string",
      "dashboard_name": "string, optional for instantiate",
      "operation": "list|read|instantiate",
      "template_id": "string, optional"
    },
    "description": "List, read, or instantiate app templates a backend serves. This tool does NOT publish or author apps \u2014 apps.json is served by the backend, so publish or update it via manage_backends (operation='add' or 'refresh' with apps_json), then instantiate here."
  },
  "manage_backends": {
    "args": {
      "apps_json": "array of app definitions (build payload)",
      "backend_id": "string, required for refresh",
      "name": "string, required for add",
      "operation": "list|add|refresh",
      "url": "string, required when adding a custom backend",
      "widgets_json": "object map widget_id -> widget definition (build payload)"
    },
    "description": "List, add, or refresh backends. operation='add' with widgets_json registers a CUSTOM backend you author: widgets_json is the widgets.json object map your backend serves (each widget definition REQUIRES name, description, and endpoint; optional type from the workspace enum table|markdown|chart|chart-highcharts|chart-vegalite|metric|pdf|html|newsfeed|omni|live_grid|ssrm_table|multi_file_viewer|advanced_charting|iframe|youtube|note|file_viewer|ssrm_advanced (default table), gridData {w,h} on a 40-column grid, params [{paramName, type text|number|date|boolean|endpoint|ticker|button|tabs|form, label, value, options, optionsEndpoint, multiSelect, ...}], and data.table.columnsDefs [{field, headerName, cellDataType, formatterFn, renderFn greenRed|titleCase|hoverCard|cellOnClick|columnColor|showCellChange, renderFnParams {actionType groupBy|sendToAgent, groupBy {paramName}}, ...}] for tables). Widget config fields: staleTime (cache ms, >=1000), refetchInterval (auto-refresh ms), runButton (boolean, adds a manual run button), source, category. Type-specific data fields: data.defaultSymbol (advanced_charting), data.wsRowIdColumn + top-level wsEndpoint (live_grid), data.updateFrequency, data.dataKey (response key holding rows). form params carry inputParams (an array of inner param definitions) plus their own submit 'endpoint' (relative path) and optional 'method' POST|PUT; 'multiple' is allowed on text params only. apps_json is the apps.json ARRAY (each app REQUIRES name and tabs {tab_id: {id, name, layout: [{i, x, y, w, h, optional state {params {..}} presets}]}}; every layout 'i' must be a widget_id the backend serves; no overlapping layout items; optional description, allowCustomization, groups [{name, type endpointParam|param|ticker, paramName, widgetIds}], prompts [string]). Invalid payloads are rejected with specific errors. operation='refresh' with widgets_json/apps_json replaces what an existing custom backend serves \u2014 use it to fix a broken custom backend."
  },
  "update_widget": {
    "args": {
      "dashboard_id": "string, optional",
      "data_args": "object, optional",
      "ui_args": "object, optional",
      "widget_id": "string, only when exactly one exists",
      "widget_uuid": "string, preferred when known"
    },
    "description": "Update widget data_args or ui_args. Do not use for layout."
  }
}

